<h1>Changelog</h1>
<h2>v0.2.0 (XXXX-XX-XX)</h2>
<ul>
    <li>The app requires the Guardian on the same system, and the Kelvin REST API and Keycloak in the domain.</li>
    <li>Sessions are now kept in an encrypted browser cookie instead of in the memory of a single
        process, so they survive a restart of the app and an app update.</li>
    <li>A session now ends at the latest eight hours after the login, even if it is used
        continuously.</li>
    <li>The Keycloak client the app logs users in with is now confidential and
        authenticates itself with a client secret generated per host.</li>
    <li>The page header shows the logged in user and a button that ends the session.</li>
</ul>

<h2>v0.1.1 (2024-04-29)</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Fix a bug, where users without school classes could cause errors in the backend.</li>
</ul>

